Z||000003||1FST2M6||05-09-2000||11:29 PM||||I deal with Turbo and Supercharged Hondas, Acuras and the like everday.  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  the best bang for the buck would be the simple V6 swap... no problems with engine management, or having to fabricate motor mounts. the VTEC actuators and solenoids are good  for their application but they are torque less wonders. Horsepower sells cars.. torque wins races. welcome to the forum. their are countless options for you 4 banger that will give you exponentialy better gains than the smaller 1.6-2.2 VTEC cars. Yes it can be done.. but why waste your money. Upgrade the injection system, air filter, header, exhaust and a decent set of tires and you'll be hanging with the best of them.. if they start SMOKING ya.. call Chris at NOPI <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  and get a nitrous kit... ||||reg||1
